Apple surprised us with the first beta of iOS 27.2 today instead of releasing an iOS 27.1 beta. Apple likely went straight to iOS 27.2 to keep <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> code under wraps for now, since we already know the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-duo-ios-27-1/">will ship with iOS 27.1</a> when it comes out in October.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27.2-Next-to-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065585" /><br/>
This beta includes Apple's revamped Health app, new languages for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI, and a handful of other useful tweaks.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="revamped_health_app">Revamped Health App</h2><br/>
The iOS 27.2 beta includes the redesigned Health app Apple showed off at its September iPhone event. The new app is organized into three main tabs: Insights, Longevity, and Browse.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063937" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/apple-ios-27-health-app-watch.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" /><br/>
Insights includes your most recent and relevant health info, such as vitals, sleep score, heart rate, and Activity Rings. Longevity shows your health data over time, offering up a Health Age calculated from activity level, VO2 max, sleep time, and other metrics.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Apple Health App Gets a HUGE Update in iOS 27.2" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/W1KpBuG0p7g" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe><em><a href="https://www.youtube.com/user/macrumors?sub_confirmation=1">Subscribe to the MacRumors YouTube channel</a> for more videos.</em></div><br/>
The Health Age feature uses in-app assessments that take advantage of the iPhone's camera. You can measure flexibility, strength, balance, and VO2 max. The revamped Health app is only available in U.S. English.<br/>
<br/>
The Health app also has a new icon.<br/>
<h2 id="call_context">Call Context</h2><br/>
Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/16/ios-27-2-could-save-your-marriage/">added anniversary alerts</a> to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> Call Context feature. If you make a phone call to someone and you have an anniversary for them set in the Contacts app, you'll see a reminder in the Phone app.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065607" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios272anniversary.jpg" alt="" width="1400" height="788" /><br/>
<h2 id="carplay">CarPlay</h2><br/>
There are themes for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/carplay/">CarPlay</a> Ultra that include options for wallpaper, gauge style, and color. Code suggests ambient lighting in supported vehicles will also match the color of the selected theme.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="siri_ai_languages">Siri AI Languages</h2><br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/16/siri-ai-new-languages-ios-27-2/">is available</a> in French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish in the iOS 27.2 beta.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="apple_tv_app">Apple TV App</h2><br/>
Apple extended <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> app profiles to the iPhone and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> in iOS 27.2. &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; app users can create profiles in the account settings section, and then swap between those profiles. Profiles only require a name, profile rating, and information about whether the user is a child.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065602" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-tv-app-profiles.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" /><br/>
Creating an account for a child limits content to a PG rating by default, but there is a customize option for more granular control. Users can select age ratings for TV shows and movies that are appropriate for the child based on their age. Profiles are useful for parents that want to hand over an iPhone or &zwnj;iPad&zwnj; to a child to watch TV content while also restricting content that's not age-appropriate.<br/>
<br/>
There's also a new option to turn on sign language interpretation when available. It can be toggled on in the TV app settings.<br/>
<h2 id="asl_facetime_api">ASL FaceTime API</h2><br/>
Back in May, Apple said it would add a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/19/new-accessibility-features-with-apple-intelligence/">new API to FaceTime</a> allowing developers who make sign language interpretation apps to add a human interpreter to an ongoing video call.<br/>
<br/>
That feature appears to be live in iOS 27.2.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="clock">Clock</h2><br/>
Apple tweaked how alarms appear in the Clock app. The a.m. and p.m. readouts are now smaller than the time.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-clock-app.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065633" /><br/>
<h2 id="music">Music</h2><br/>
In the Music app, some of the red accents have been removed. The Play and Shuffle buttons in Library are black instead of red, as are all of the icons next to the Library sections.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-apple-music-design.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065634" /><br/>
<h2 id="siri">Siri</h2><br/>
App Access in the &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; section of the Settings app is now named "Excluded Apps." Tapping on "Add Apps" brings up a list so multiple apps can be excluded at once. Apps previously had to be excluded one by one.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-excluded-apps-siri.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065635" /><br/>
Adding an app to the Exclude list prevents it from showing up in &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;, Search, and suggestions.<br/>
<h2 id="podcasts">Podcasts</h2><br/>
Apple renamed Up Next to New Episodes, with a Continue Playing option directly below it.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-podcasts.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065636" /><br/>
<h2 id="app_tracking_transparency">App Tracking Transparency</h2><br/>
